[Term]
id: ENVO:01000318
name: extreme high temperature environment
def: "An extreme high temperature environment is a high temperature environment in which entities are exposed to temperatures above 80 degrees Celsius." []
comment: The lower threshold, 80 degrees Celsius, is derived from the definition of the obsolete class "extreme high temperature habitat" which this class replaces.
is_a: ENVO:01000305 ! high temperature environment

[Term]
id: ENVO:01000319
name: rocky slope
def: "A rocky slope is a slope which has a surface primarily composed of rock." []
is_a: ENVO:00002000 ! slope

