[Term]
id: ENVO:2000034
name: geothermal energy
def: "Thermal energy which propagates through a solid (typically rocky) astronomical body." []
comment: Often, this term is used specifically for thermal energy spreading from heat sources (e.g. magma chambers, the planetary core) within the Earth. However, it is also used for extraterrestrial bodies.
is_a: ENVO:2000032 ! thermal energy
created_by: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165
creation_date: 2018-11-03T20:47:30Z

