[Term]
id: NCBITaxon:4538
name: Oryza glaberrima
def: "A domesticated rice species commonly known as African rice." []
comment: It was first domesticated and grown in West Africa, and was brought to the Americas by enslaved West African rice farmers. It is now largely a subsistence crop, rarely sold in markets even in West Africa. While it has been partly replaced by higher-yielding Asian rice, and the number of varieties grown is declining, it persists, making up an estimated 20% of rice grown in West Africa.\n\nIn comparison to Asian rice, it is hardy, pest-resistant, low-labour, suited to a variety of African conditions, filling, and has a distinct nutty flavour. \nCrossbreeding between African and Asian rice is difficult, but there exist some crosses.
synonym: "African rice" EXACT []
synonym: "Oryza glaberrima Steud." NARROW []
synonym: "Oryza glaberrima Steudel" NARROW []
synonym: "red rice" RELATED []
