[Term]
id: NCIT:C16818
name: Mammography
def: "A type of radiography used specifically to examine breast tissue. The procedure utilizes a low-dose of x-rays or radiation to generate an image. A mammography exam or mammogram, is used as a screening tool to detect early breast cancer in women experiencing no symptoms and to detect and diagnose breast disease." [] {NCIT:P378="NCI"}
