[Term]
id: NCIT:C17009
name: Poverty
def: "A subjective and comparative term describing a lack of sufficient wealth (usually understood as capital, money, material goods, or resources especially natural resources) to live what is understood in a society as a \"normal\" life: for instance, to be capable of raising a healthy family, and especially educating children and participating in society. A person living in this condition of poverty is said to be poor. The meaning of \"sufficient\" varies widely across the different political and economic areas of the world." [] {NCIT:P378="NCI"}
