[Term]
id: PO:0030109
name: hesperidium fruit
namespace: plant_anatomy
def: "A berry fruit (PO:0030108) which develops from a superior gynoecium (PO:0009062) and at maturity comprises a thickened exocarp (PO:0009085), thickened mesocarp (PO:0009087), and endocarp (PO:0009086), and has as parts juice sacs (PO:0006013) on a carpel adaxial epidermis (PO:0025618)." []
comment: A hesperidium fruit (PO:0030109) develops from a superior gynoecium (PO:0009062), and therefore is not surrounded by receptacle (PO:0009064) tissue. Examples: orange, grapefruit, lemon, and lime (Citrus spp.).
synonym: "citrus fruit (exact)" EXACT []
synonym: "hesperide (exact, German)" EXACT []
synonym: "hesperidio (exact, Spanish)" EXACT []
synonym: "hesperidium (exact)" EXACT []
